oad and reshape:\n./briefing.md:15:`out$data` is the analysis-ready long format; `out$labels` maps attribute ids (`att1`…`att7`) to their human-readable names and levels.\n./briefing.md:20:2. `summary.md` — a tidy design summary: respondents, tasks per respondent, profiles per task, the seven attributes with their level counts (human-readable names from `out$labels`), and a randomization balance check (level frequencies within each attribute).\n./briefing.md:21:3. `figures/level-frequencies.png` — ONE descriptive figure of attribute-level frequencies, 300+ dpi. No in-plot title: the figure's one-sentence caption goes under the figure reference in `summary.md`.\n./briefing.md:32:- **Randomized choice tasks per respondent:** 8 (plus one repeated, flipped version of task 1 for reliability checking)\n./briefing.md:33:- **Profiles per randomized task:** 2\n./briefing.md:34:- **Analysis-ready profile rows:** 6,400\n./briefing.md:41:| Presidential Vote (2020) | 3 |\n./briefing.md:44:| Total Daily Driving Time for Commuting and Errands | 4 |\n./briefing.md:48:## Randomization balance\n./briefing.md:50:The table gives the observed frequency of every attribute level across the 6,400 randomized profile rows; the equal-allocation target is shown for comparison.\n./briefing.md:52:| Attribute | Level | Frequency | Share | Equal-allocation target | Deviation |\n./briefing.md:57:| Presidential Vote (2020) | 30% Democrat, 70% Republican | 2,144 | 33.5% | 2,133 | +11 |\n./briefing.md:58:| Presidential Vote (2020) | 50% Democrat, 50% Republican | 2,147 | 33.5% | 2,133 | +14 |\n./briefing.md:59:| Presidential Vote (2020) | 70% Democrat, 30% Republican | 2,109 | 33.0% | 2,133 | -24 |\n./briefing.md:66:| Total Daily Driving Time for Commuting and Errands | 10 min | 1,601 | 25.0% | 1,600 | +1 |\n./briefing.md:67:| Total Daily Driving Time for Commuting and Errands | 25 min | 1,724 | 26.9% | 1,600 | +124 |\n./briefing.md:68:| Total Daily Driving Time for Commuting and Errands | 45 min | 1,527 | 23.9% | 1,600 | -73 |\n./briefing.md:69:| Total Daily Driving Time for Commuting and Errands | 75 min | 1,548 | 24.2% | 1,600 | -52 |\n./briefing.md:71:| Type of Place | City, more residential area | 1,032 | 16.1% | 1,067 | -35 |\n./briefing.md:79:![Attribute-level frequencies](figures/level-frequencies.png)\n./briefing.md:81:*Figure 1. Attribute-level assignment frequencies; dashed vertical lines mark the equal-allocation frequency implied by each attribute's number of levels.*\n./briefing.md:105:    panel.grid.major.y = element_blank(),\n./briefing.md:106:    panel.grid.minor = element_blank(),\n./briefing.md:121:attribute_ids <- paste0(\"att\", 1:7)\n./briefing.md:123:if (!all(attribute_ids %in% names(dat))) {\n./briefing.md:127:respondent_n <- length(unique(dat$id))\n./briefing.md:128:task_n <- length(unique(dat$task))\n./briefing.md:129:profile_n <- length(unique(dat$profile))\n./briefing.md:131:if (nrow(dat) != respondent_n * task_n * profile_n) {\n./briefing.md:132:  stop(\"Profile rows are not a complete respondent-by-task-by-profile design.\")\n./briefing.md:135:attribute_info <- unique(labels[c(\"attribute_id\", \"attribute\")])\n./briefing.md:136:attribute_info <- attribute_info[match(attribute_ids, attribute_info$attribute_id), ]\n./briefing.md:138:  attribute_info$attribute_id,\n./briefing.md:139:  function(attribute_id) sum(labels$attribute_id == attribute_id),\n./briefing.md:145:  lapply(attribute_ids, function(attribute_id) {\n./briefing.md:146:    attribute_labels <- labels[labels$attribute_id == attribute_id, ]\n./briefing.md:148:      as.character(dat[[attribute_id]]),\n./briefing.md:149:      levels = attribute_labels$level_id\n./briefing.md:152:      attribute_id = attribute_id,\n./briefing.md:175:dir.create(\"figures\", showWarnings = FALSE, recursive = TRUE)\n./briefing.md:187:    linewidth = 0.35\n./briefing.md:189:  geom_col(width = 0.72, show.legend = FALSE) +\n./briefing.md:194:    labeller = labeller(attribute = label_wrap_gen(width